Like, all I needed was myself,
you know, I needed my mom

00:54:30.770 --> 00:54:31.603
to a degree.

00:54:31.603 --> 00:54:33.097
And then I was old enough
that that became me,

00:54:33.097 --> 00:54:36.853
and so at some level, I
just, here's my big thing.

00:54:38.190 --> 00:54:40.460
You're this thing from me,

00:54:40.460 --> 00:54:42.210
like thing about our conversations,

00:54:43.680 --> 00:54:45.590
I'm just not interested
in the people that boo

00:54:45.590 --> 00:54:46.865
in the second quarter.

00:54:46.865 --> 00:54:47.770
(Matt chuckling)

00:54:47.770 --> 00:54:51.370
Like for me, this is my
thinking on judgment or hate

00:54:51.370 --> 00:54:52.730
along the way.

00:54:52.730 --> 00:54:56.290
If those people are right
when it goes to triple zero

00:54:56.290 --> 00:54:59.760
of the game, then I have
to concede that truth.

00:54:59.760 --> 00:55:02.150
If they were right that
I was full of shit,

00:55:02.150 --> 00:55:05.175
not as smart as I think,
like, whatever it may be,

00:55:05.175 --> 00:55:09.210
and it ends, I've had my career
and I was not successful,

00:55:09.210 --> 00:55:10.720
I over-leveraged, I went to zero,

00:55:10.720 --> 00:55:13.030
I had to work for somebody
one day, I would just,

00:55:13.030 --> 00:55:16.140
you know, I don't like
shaking people's hands

00:55:16.140 --> 00:55:17.860
after you lose a game of basketball.

00:55:17.860 --> 00:55:19.520
But I do it because I lost.

00:55:19.520 --> 00:55:20.623
And that's the facts.

00:55:20.623 --> 00:55:23.410
- But that capacity to
do that is super human.

00:55:23.410 --> 00:55:24.695
- But I mean--
- I don't know where

00:55:24.695 --> 00:55:25.528
it comes from.

00:55:25.528 --> 00:55:26.361
- But I don't think it has to be.

00:55:26.361 --> 00:55:28.599
And that's why I'm trying to bring more,

00:55:28.599 --> 00:55:29.432
like it's actually practical.

00:55:29.432 --> 00:55:31.202
It's the same reason
that I don't get excited.

00:55:31.202 --> 00:55:34.300
The Jets were beating the
Browns 14 nothing at half time

00:55:34.300 --> 00:55:35.133
the other day.

00:55:35.133 --> 00:55:36.080
We lost.

00:55:36.080 --> 00:55:37.420
Like, just 'cause I'm winning,

00:55:37.420 --> 00:55:40.080
like back to what Nathan
was worried about,

00:55:40.080 --> 00:55:44.218
just 'cause I'm conceivably
winning right this minute?

00:55:44.218 --> 00:55:47.230
Everything could start
going downhill tomorrow.

00:55:47.230 --> 00:55:48.390
And if it does?

00:55:48.390 --> 00:55:49.400
Then I lost.

00:55:49.400 --> 00:55:50.876
And it goes in a lot of ways.

00:55:50.876 --> 00:55:54.660
It not only goes professionally,
and this is where I don't

00:55:54.660 --> 00:55:55.835
think people are being thoughtful.

00:55:55.835 --> 00:55:58.000
I don't just score on the money part.

00:55:58.000 --> 00:55:59.690
A lot of people that boo us along the way

00:55:59.690 --> 00:56:02.683
are just talking about money, right?

00:56:04.000 --> 00:56:06.720
Matt Lowers brand looks different today

00:56:06.720 --> 00:56:08.480
than it did a year-and-a-half ago.

00:56:08.480 --> 00:56:10.830
He was making 20 plus
million, 30 million last year.

00:56:10.830 --> 00:56:13.470
So to me, back to the empathy thing?

00:56:13.470 --> 00:56:17.070
I'm going, I know it, you know
this way better than most.

00:56:17.070 --> 00:56:18.960
Very few people know it as well as you do.

00:56:18.960 --> 00:56:22.290
I will always leave economics on the table

00:56:22.290 --> 00:56:25.280
because I don't believe being
the greatest entrepreneur

00:56:25.280 --> 00:56:27.240
of this generation is just the person

00:56:27.240 --> 00:56:29.440
that made the most money.

00:56:29.440 --> 00:56:33.510
Like, the reason I think
I can beat Zux and Elon

00:56:33.510 --> 00:56:36.830
and Sarah Blakely and
others is 'cause for me,

00:56:36.830 --> 00:56:39.080
and I get to judge 'cause that's my life,

00:56:39.080 --> 00:56:41.100
the greatest entrepreneur of
this generation is not only

00:56:41.100 --> 00:56:42.776
somebody, and I do think
you have to succeed,

00:56:42.776 --> 00:56:45.151
I do think I have to make
lots of money 'cause that's

00:56:45.151 --> 00:56:46.519
the game of an entrepreneur,

00:56:46.519 --> 00:56:49.630
but the one who brings the most
value to the entrepreneurial

00:56:49.630 --> 00:56:52.291
space, yeah, that's interesting to me.

00:56:52.291 --> 00:56:53.124
- I mean, you put something
out the other day.

00:56:53.124 --> 00:56:53.957
Your post, I forgot how you worded it,

00:56:53.957 --> 00:56:56.070
but you said focus on what you do well

00:56:56.070 --> 00:56:58.891
because other people focus on
what you're not doing well.

00:56:58.891 --> 00:56:59.799
- [Gary] That's right.

00:56:59.799 --> 00:57:00.810
- Well, it's interesting,
but a lot of people

00:57:00.810 --> 00:57:02.538
take the opposite approach.

00:57:02.538 --> 00:57:03.371
I gotta mitigate my downside.

00:57:03.371 --> 00:57:04.204
I gotta work at what I'm not good at--

00:57:04.204 --> 00:57:05.200
- Because they--

00:57:05.200 --> 00:57:06.362
- [Matt] You're all into that.

00:57:06.362 --> 00:57:07.195
- I'll tell you why.

00:57:07.195 --> 00:57:08.980
'Cause they don't realize
that whoever they're scared

00:57:08.980 --> 00:57:11.355
is in control of them is not
as in control as they think.

00:57:11.355 --> 00:57:16.355
The Board of Directors, the
CEO, the 51% equity partner.

00:57:17.120 --> 00:57:20.910
Yes, in the micro of the
moment, definitely not.

00:57:20.910 --> 00:57:22.163
In the macro of life.

00:57:23.710 --> 00:57:24.644
- Alright.

00:57:24.644 --> 00:57:25.477
- Question of the day.

00:57:25.477 --> 00:57:27.370
Every guest gets to ask
the question of the day.

00:57:27.370 --> 00:57:29.553
So what question, do you Matt,
have for the Veyner nation?

00:57:29.553 --> 00:57:32.216
This is an amazing opportunity
for you to get some insights.

00:57:32.216 --> 00:57:33.470
- So explain it a little more.

00:57:33.470 --> 00:57:35.590
- Well, I'm thrilled to know
you don't watch the show

00:57:35.590 --> 00:57:36.423
at all--

00:57:36.423 --> 00:57:37.256
(Matt laughing)

00:57:37.256 --> 00:57:40.390
When I have a guest, when
I have a guest he or she

00:57:40.390 --> 00:57:43.610
gets to ask a question and
then thousands of comments

00:57:43.610 --> 00:57:46.180
come on Facebook and
YouTube, and some guests

00:57:46.180 --> 00:57:48.640
ask silly things like
what's your favorite color.

00:57:48.640 --> 00:57:50.610
Others are very strategic 'cause
they're trying to actually

00:57:50.610 --> 00:57:53.278
literally get an insight at
that moment of like a trend

00:57:53.278 --> 00:57:54.500
or a thing.

00:57:54.500 --> 00:57:56.276
Or then some people are
trying to scratch to itch

00:57:56.276 --> 00:57:58.630
on some opinions that they're
debating on themselves

00:57:58.630 --> 00:57:59.463
right now.

00:57:59.463 --> 00:58:00.392
- Okay.

00:58:00.392 --> 00:58:01.225
- So what's your question.

00:58:01.225 --> 00:58:03.730
- Alright, what's a product
that I don't know about

00:58:03.730 --> 00:58:06.210
that you think I should know
about that is going to be

00:58:06.210 --> 00:58:08.980
massive that's not on the radar right now?

00:58:08.980 --> 00:58:09.987
- I like that.

00:58:09.987 --> 00:58:12.197
- So I can buy it and
help make Gary richer.

00:58:12.197 --> 00:58:13.060
(Gary laughing)

00:58:13.060 --> 00:58:14.000
- Thank you, brother.

00:58:14.000 --> 00:58:15.341
Thanks for being on the show.

00:58:15.341 --> 00:58:16.174
- Thanks.

00:58:16.174 --> 00:58:17.007
- You keep asking questions.

00:58:17.007 --> 00:58:18.188
We'll keep answering them.

00:58:18.188 --> 00:58:21.771
(exciting rhythmic music)

